eometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c49" value="ois" style="endArrow=open;endSize=10;html=1;rounded=0;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.8;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c9" target="c42"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c50" value="All networking is written inside the panel (&lt;b&gt;GamePanelLAN.java, lines 19–22 and 63–171&lt;/b&gt;):&lt;br&gt;4 socket and stream fields, and 6 of its 10 methods (connect, createReciver, createServer, sendData, closeFrame, resetSockets) work on them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The game screen depends directly on four java.net / java.io classes, so the game and the connection cannot be changed or tested separately." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="220" width="560" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c51" value="" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.25;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c50" target="c9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c52" value="sendData (lines 122–133):&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;oos.writeObject(oldPosition);&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;oos.writeObject(newPosition);&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;createReciver (lines 79–104): a thread calls&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ois.readObject()&lt;/font&gt; twice, then threadMoveChess(new, old).&lt;br&gt;connect + createServer (lines 63–120): join, or else host and wait." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1220" y="220" width="560" height="120" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxC